// lexdb over TNS: the fourth bug slice (design/lexdb-robust.md, "The fourth bug slice"; KNOWN-ISSUES.md), checked against Oracle Database Free
// 23.26 (gen_oracle.py --check tns_bugs4): a NUMBER, NUMBER(p) or NUMBER(p,s) foreign key to a NUMBER GENERATED AS IDENTITY key (lexdb's bigint),
// NUMBER(10) to INTEGER, INTEGER to NUMBER, both ways: a child's 5 and 5.0 find the parent's 5, 5.5 and numbers past bigint's range find none
// (ORA-02291), NULL, INSERT ... SELECT with a bad row late, UPDATE of the child, DELETE and UPDATE of the parent (ORA-02292, ON DELETE CASCADE, SET
// NULL), ADD CONSTRAINT over rows (ORA-02298), the types Oracle refuses (ORA-02267); a view and a session's first read after the function the view
// calls is dropped (ORA-04063, ORA-04067) and USER_OBJECTS.STATUS of the view; a function or procedure created with compilation errors (INVALID,
// USER_ERRORS, ORA-06575 and ORA-04063 when called); SESSIONTIMEZONE after ALTER SESSION SET TIME_ZONE to a region; TO_CHAR of a TIMESTAMP WITH
// LOCAL TIME ZONE with the zone elements (ORA-01821). Each statement runs with set lexdb_batch = off (the row engine) and on: "same" and the
// answer, or DIFFERENT and both.
